[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says one bug: the parser reads dates month first. Read report by report,
the ticket holds three problems. Each one now has its own ticket, with the reports it covers.

<ProblemTable
  ticket={4471}
  issues={{
    parser: 'https://github.com/pavani06/megadev-challenge/issues/1',
    hint: 'https://github.com/pavani06/megadev-challenge/issues/2',
    'one-day': 'https://github.com/pavani06/megadev-challenge/issues/3',
  }}
/>

<Callout kind="warn">
Not one fix. The parser fix leaves the other two broken: the booking-v3 hint keeps asking for
the month first, and the one-day moves have no month in them to flip.
</Callout>

## The three problems

**`parser`: the shared parser reads every date month first.** Our tenants write the day first, so
"7 April" comes out as 4 July. Every channel, every tenant. This is what #4471 already says.

**`hint`: booking-v3's date field asks for the wrong order.** Under its date field the v3 form
prints `MM/DD/YYYY`. People type what it shows, month first, and the form reads it the tenant's
way, day first. Only reports sent through the form of a tenant on booking-v3. The parser fix does
not touch it; the hint does.

**`one-day`: a date one day off.** No day and month swap in these, a shift of one day: "Invite says
Tuesday 12 May. Calendar says Monday 11 May." (R-41202), "Client in Lisbon got Tuesday. Client in
Toronto got Monday." (R-41344), "The invite arrived before I made the booking." (R-41236). That reads
as a time zone or day-boundary bug, not a date-order one. The desk had already listed these in
`desk-notes.json`; the cause table filed them under `parser` because of their tenant.

## How the count is made

- One id, one report: the export repeats rows across its pages, and the repeats are dropped.
- `parser` and `hint` come from `causes.ts` (tenant locale, booking form and channel), never from
  the intake tag. Intake guesses from the reporter's browser and disagrees with the tenant both ways.
- `one-day` is the desk's own list in `desk-notes.json`; each of those bodies was read.
- The subject line does not tell them apart: "Month and day swapped?" heads reports of all three
  problems, so merging on subject ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)) put them in one ticket.

Every number on this page is computed at render time from `src/lib/data/`. The tickets carry the
same counts and the list of report ids.

